downloading SRA data on ISAAC
-> go to NCBI SRA database and search your target organism
-> at the top of the page select "Send to:" -> "File" -> format: "Full XML" -> "Create File"
-> open your xml file in excell, or similar, and choose your desired organisms
-> in your terminal, or code editor, ssh into ISAAC datatransfer node dtn1 or dtn2.isaac.utk.edu
bash:> ssh <netID>@dtn1.isaac.utk.edu
-> cd or mkdir to your desired directory for sra data
-> create a file "SraAccList.txt" and insert your desired SRA numbers from the XML file
bash:> module load sra-tools/3.4.1
bash:> prefetch --option-file SraAccList.txt
-> add flag " --max-size <amount>G " before the second flag in order to bypass thee built in 20G limit
